<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
        xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
        xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
            http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-latest.xsd">

    <!--
      Wave 03 "PRIME": the first widget returns to the board: music (DESIGN §10.2).

      The order of return was already set by the 0480 seed: the canvas is tuned on an empty screen, the widgets
      arrive one at a time. Music goes first not alphabetically: it is the only tile
      that changes by itself, without a click and without choosing a day: the playing track is updated
      by polling. Behind glass that blurs the canvas ribbon under it, a live widget
      shows the wave's material more honestly than a static one.

      Composition. The switcher stops being the centre: it is not content but a
      control, and it has nothing to share the optical centre with a widget. The pair lines up in
      a column on one axis: music on top, below it after a spacer the row of wave cards.
      The column is raised one row above the geometric centre: the screen's optical centre
      lies above the middle.

      The switcher's width 5 → 6 columns, and this is not about the card size but about the AXIS. A tile
      an odd number of columns wide cannot centre on the even 40 grid: the five
      sat on column 19.5, music (12 columns) exactly on column 20, and on a 1536 screen
      the two glass rectangles' centres diverged by 19px. Noticeable: a column of two
      tiles reads along a shared axis, and a half-column miss is seen before the sizes themselves.
      The six lands on column 20 exactly.

      Music gets a frame wider and taller than its default (12x7 against 8x5): the card inside hugs
      its content and centres itself (see `MusicTile`), so the wide frame does not stretch
      the glass: it only gives the recent list a vertical and the long track title a width
      at which no marquee is needed.

      This wave's per-tile Playwright baselines are still untouched (the canon is wave 01).
    -->
    <changeSet id="0530-wave-03-music-tile" author="danchuo">
        <sql><![CDATA[
UPDATE theme
SET layout = jsonb_set(
        jsonb_set(
            jsonb_set(layout, '{tiles,music}', $J${"col": 15, "row": 8, "colSpan": 12, "rowSpan": 7}$J$::jsonb),
            '{tiles,waveSwitcher}',
            $J${"col": 18, "row": 16, "colSpan": 6, "rowSpan": 4}$J$::jsonb
        ),
        '{mobileOrder}',
        $J$["music", "waveSwitcher"]$J$::jsonb
    )
WHERE key = 'wave-03';
        ]]></sql>
        <rollback><![CDATA[
UPDATE theme
SET layout = jsonb_set(
        jsonb_set(
            jsonb_set(layout, '{tiles,music}', $J${"hidden": true}$J$::jsonb),
            '{tiles,waveSwitcher}',
            $J${"col": 18, "row": 13, "colSpan": 5, "rowSpan": 4}$J$::jsonb
        ),
        '{mobileOrder}',
        $J$["waveSwitcher"]$J$::jsonb
    )
WHERE key = 'wave-03';
        ]]></rollback>
    </changeSet>
</databaseChangeLog>
